{"metadata":{"title":"Using IvorExtern","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"IvorExtern"}],"roleHeading":"Article"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"IvorExtern connects ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/eBardX\/IvorModel","type":"reference"},{"text":" works to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"files in other formats. Each format is handled by a lower-level Ivor package,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which IvorExtern drives on your behalf:","type":"text"}]},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Format","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Filename extensions","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Time basis"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Pitch notation","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Built on"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ABC File"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"abc"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Beat","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Standard"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"IvorABC"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Guido Score File"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"gmn"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Beat"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Standard"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"IvorGMN","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"JohnnySonic Score File","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"dkm","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"johnnysonic","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Beat"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Absolute, keyboard"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"IvorDKM"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Standard MIDI File","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"mid","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"midi","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"smf","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Beat, wall"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keyboard"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"IvorSMF"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"MusicXML Document","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"musicxml"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"xml"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Beat"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Standard","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"IvorMXL"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Compressed MusicXML Document","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mxl"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Beat","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Standard"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"IvorMXL"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"header":"row","type":"table","alignments":["left","left","left","left","left"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The core types are ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorExtern\/documentation\/IvorExtern\/ImportFileFormat","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorExtern\/documentation\/IvorExtern\/ExportFileFormat","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", which read","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and write files, and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorExtern\/documentation\/IvorExtern\/WorkPerformance","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", which turns a work into timed MIDI","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"channel messages.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Finding a format","anchor":"Finding-a-format"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A format is looked up by a filename extension or a MIME type, such as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"document picker or a URL gives you:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let abc  = ImportFileFormat.importFileFormat(for: \"abc\")","let midi = ExportFileFormat.exportFileFormat(for: \"audio\/midi\")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" for a tag no format supports. The type properties"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"supportedFilenameExtensions"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"supportedMIMETypes"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"supportedTimeBases"},{"type":"text","text":", and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"supportedPitchNotations"},{"type":"text","text":" list what is supported across every format, and their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"preferred…"},{"type":"text","text":" counterparts give one extension or MIME type per format, for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"building a file type list. A format value also has a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorExtern\/documentation\/IvorExtern\/ImportFileFormat\/displayName","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and its own extensions, MIME types, time bases,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and pitch notations."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Importing","type":"heading","text":"Importing","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorExtern\/documentation\/IvorExtern\/ImportFileFormat\/read(from:options:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" reads every work a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FileWrapper"},{"type":"text","text":" holds — an ABC"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"file can hold a whole tunebook — as an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorExtern\/documentation\/IvorExtern\/ImportResult","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let result = try ImportFileFormat.importFileFormat(for: \"abc\")!","    .read(from: FileWrapper(url: url))","let works = result.works"],"syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each work comes back in the time basis and pitch notation of its format, as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the table above shows. It holds whatever the file records of its parts, notes,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dynamics, instruments, and pan positions, and of its descriptive information —"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"titles, credits, rights, and remarks — in the work’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"info"},{"text":". A work read from a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Standard MIDI File whose times were measured in SMPTE frames reports","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Work.hasMIDITimeCode"},{"text":", so that writing it back keeps the same division.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorExtern\/documentation\/IvorExtern\/ImportOptions","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" adjusts how a format reads: its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorExtern\/documentation\/IvorExtern\/ImportOptions\/pedalSimplification","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" simplifies each imported pedal table. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"format ignores any option it doesn’t use, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorExtern\/documentation\/IvorExtern\/ImportFileFormat\/supportedOptions","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" lists the ones it does.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Exporting","type":"heading","text":"Exporting"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A format can write a work only in a time basis and pitch notation it supports.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorExtern\/documentation\/IvorExtern\/ExportFileFormat\/canWrite(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" checks a work, and IvorModel’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"convert(timeBasis:pitchNotation:context:dropsUnconvertibleNotes:appliesFermataHolds:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" converts","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one that doesn’t fit:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let midi = ExportFileFormat.exportFileFormat(for: \"mid\")!","var work = works[0]                        \/\/ beat time, standard pitch","","if !midi.canWrite(work) {","    work = try work.convert(timeBasis: .beat, pitchNotation: .keyboard)!","}","","let file = try midi.write(works: [work]).file   \/\/ a FileWrapper"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorExtern\/documentation\/IvorExtern\/ExportFileFormat\/write(works:options:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" writes one or more works to a ","type":"text"},{"code":"FileWrapper","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ready to save or share, as an ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorExtern\/documentation\/IvorExtern\/ExportResult","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Warnings","text":"Warnings"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Reading and writing both report what a format couldn’t carry over exactly, as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorExtern\/documentation\/IvorExtern\/ExternWarning","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" values in ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorExtern\/documentation\/IvorExtern\/ImportResult\/warnings","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorExtern\/documentation\/IvorExtern\/ExportResult\/warnings","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":": one per kind of loss in each work, with a count. ABC","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has no figure after a note, for example, so writing one moves it before the next","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"note and reports ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorExtern\/documentation\/IvorExtern\/ExternWarning\/Kind-swift.enum\/movedFigureAfterNote","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"; and it has no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"caesura, so writing one drops it and reports","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorExtern\/documentation\/IvorExtern\/ExternWarning\/Kind-swift.enum\/droppedCaesura","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". A warning never stops a read or write.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Ornaments-in-ABC","text":"Ornaments in ABC"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"ABC reads and writes grace groups (with chords in braces, the slash, and a tie","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"into the main note), trills, both mordents, rolled chords, abcm2ps’s tremolo","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"marks (","type":"text"},{"code":"!\/!","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to ","type":"text"},{"code":"!\/\/\/!","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"!trem1!","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"code":"!trem4!","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" between two notes), and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fermatas — on a note, on a rest, or before a bar line, where it becomes a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fermata mark over the last event. A lone grace note is an eighth and each of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"group a sixteenth, whatever ","type":"text"},{"code":"L:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" says, as the ABC renderers read them."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Keys","type":"heading","text":"Keys"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A beat-time work’s key table comes in from every format that has keys and goes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"back out to it. Each entry is a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Key"},{"text":": atonal, diatonic (with the mode the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"source names, or none where it names none), or custom. A key a format records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"but Ivor can’t represent (one with a double sharp or flat, or a microtonal","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"alteration) is left out on import, and so is one that only repeats the key","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"before it. Mode names are normalized on round trip: ABC’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"K:Aaeo","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" comes back"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as ","type":"text"},{"code":"K:Am","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and MusicXML’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"<mode>ionian<\/mode>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as ","type":"text"},{"code":"<mode>major<\/mode>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Format"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Reads","type":"text"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Writes","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Loses","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"MIDI","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Key signature meta events of the first track that has any, each as major or minor"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A meta event at each key, on the first track","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A custom key, written as its nearest diatonic signature; modes other than minor, and no mode, which read back as major; an atonal key, written as C major"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"MusicXML"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<key>"},{"type":"text","text":" of each part’s first staff, traditional or not, along the play order; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<mode>none<\/mode>"},{"type":"text","text":" as atonal"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<key>"},{"text":" at each key, at a measure’s start or in the middle","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"<key-octave>","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"ABC","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"K:"},{"type":"text","text":" fields, in the header and inline, along the play order; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"K:none"},{"type":"text","text":" as atonal"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"K:"},{"type":"text","text":" and inline "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[K:…]"},{"type":"text","text":", with every note’s accidental written against the key and the bar"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No mode, written as major; no key at all, written as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"K:C"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Guido","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\key"},{"text":": a number of fifths (no mode), a key name (major or minor), or a free key","type":"text"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\\key"},{"type":"text","text":": a key name for major or minor, a number of fifths otherwise, or a free key for a custom key"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Modes other than major and minor; an atonal key, written as no sharps or flats"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"JohnnySonic","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"—"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"—","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every key","type":"text"}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row","alignments":["left","left","left","left"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorExtern\/documentation\/IvorExtern\/ExportOptions","type":"reference"},{"text":" adjusts how a format writes. The formats that write sound —","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a Standard MIDI File and a JohnnySonic score — render the work first (see","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"IvorModel’s "},{"code":"Work.rendered(options:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), so its grace notes, trills, mordents,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tremolos and rolls become the notes that sound, and its fermatas and caesuras"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"become time; "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorExtern\/documentation\/IvorExtern\/ExportOptions\/fermataMode"},{"type":"text","text":" says how, slowing the tempo over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each hold by default. A Standard MIDI File also marks each fermata with a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"marker meta event, in every mode. The "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorExtern\/documentation\/IvorExtern\/MIDIExportOptions"},{"type":"text","text":" of a Standard MIDI"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"File give the ticks per quarter note for a beat-time work, and the frame rate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and ticks per frame for a wall-time one. A format ignores any option it doesn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"use, and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorExtern\/documentation\/IvorExtern\/ExportFileFormat\/supportedOptions"},{"type":"text","text":" lists the ones it does."}]},{"anchor":"Playing-a-work","text":"Playing a work","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorExtern\/documentation\/IvorExtern\/WorkPerformance"},{"text":" is a work as a MIDI player plays it: every part’s channel","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"messages, each at its time in the work, in the order they are sent. It is made","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"from a work in keyboard pitch and wall time — the initializer returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"any other — and, optionally, a realization from IvorModel that says what each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instrument sounds as. A performance plays the notes as they stand, so render"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the work first, while it’s still in beat time, then convert it:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let rendered    = try work.rendered().work","let playable    = try rendered.convert(timeBasis: .wall, pitchNotation: .keyboard)!","let performance = WorkPerformance(work: playable)!","","performance.duration        \/\/ the time of the last event","performance.events          \/\/ bank selects, program changes, pan, expression, notes, …"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Without a realization, each instrument sounds as the General MIDI instrument"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its name matches. Event times are exact "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WallTime"},{"type":"text","text":" values, never floating-point"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"seconds, so events at the same moment stay together; at the same time,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"note-offs come first, then bank selects, program changes, pan, expression,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other controllers, and note-ons."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each part plays on a channel of its own, given in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorExtern\/documentation\/IvorExtern\/WorkPerformance\/partChannels"},{"text":", unless an instrument’s assignment moves it;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorExtern\/documentation\/IvorExtern\/WorkPerformance\/partChannelSets"},{"text":" lists every channel each part plays on.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Given an output for each part,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorExtern\/documentation\/IvorExtern\/WorkPerformance\/channelOutputs(forPartOutputs:)"},{"text":" returns an output for each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"channel, in the form a MIDI router such as IvorConnect’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"MIDIRouter","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" takes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"General MIDI helpers","anchor":"General-MIDI-helpers"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"IvorExtern also extends a few IvorModel and IvorMIDI types with the General MIDI"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"knowledge its formats need:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Instrument.generalMIDIInstrument"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the General MIDI Level 1 instrument"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose name an instrument’s name matches, if any."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Patch.generalMIDIName","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the General MIDI name of a patch’s sound."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MIDIPatch(instrument:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MIDIPatch(patch:)"},{"type":"text","text":" give the bank and program"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that select an instrument or a patch."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"text":"Error handling","type":"heading","anchor":"Error-handling","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Thrown errors conform to ","type":"text"},{"code":"EnhancedError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/eBardX\/XestiTools","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"): each has a ","type":"text"},{"code":"category","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"IvorExtern\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and a human-readable ","type":"text"},{"code":"message","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Each also has a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cause"},{"type":"text","text":", holding"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the error of the lower-level package that failed, if